From ede90ac0de59fe5334e308278605879c6ec40e9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yaegerbomb42 <yaeger.james42@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:28:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(runtime): steer an active run into the same Claude
 session

- RuntimeManager.steer(): cancel the active run with reason 'superseded',
  start a new run resuming its sessionId with the prompt prefixed
  'User interrupted: '; queued items stay queued; a run.steered event
  links the old and new runIds for the timeline
- track the live session id from run.started so mid-run steer resumes
  the exact Claude session
- POST /api/runtime/tasks {action:'steer', prompt} -> {runId, steeredFrom}
- InputBar: while busy, Enter shows a 'Steer now' / 'Queue after' chip
  (Steer is the default, Esc cancels); App wires it to the steer endpoint
